      "body": "## Summary\n\n`MultimodalRotaryEmbedding.forward` computes RoPE angles with a batched fp32 matmul (`inv_freq_expanded @ seq_expanded`). cuBLAS may execute this in TF32, which is the default in NGC/NeMo containers (`TORCH_ALLOW_TF32_CUBLAS_OVERRIDE=1`) and whenever `torch.backends.cuda.matmul.allow_tf32 = True`. TF32 keeps only 11 mantissa bits, causing angle errors of several radians at positions above ~2048.\n\nThis replaces the matmul with broadcasting element-wise multiplication (`seq[..., None].float() * self.inv_freq`), which uses the fp32 ALU and is immune to the TF32 matmul override. The base `RotaryEmbedding` class already uses `torch.outer` (element-wise), so this brings `MultimodalRotaryEmbedding` in line.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `megatron/core/models/common/embeddings/rotary_pos_embedding.py`: replace the 4-line matmul sequence (expand + matmul + transpose) with a single broadcast multiply\n- `tests/unit_tests/transformer/test_rope.py`: add `test_forward_precision_under_tf32` regression test that enables TF32 and checks angle precision against an fp64 reference\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [ ] Existing `TestMultimodalRotaryEmbedding` tests pass (shape, dtype, device)\n- [ ] New `test_forward_precision_under_tf32`: enables TF32, runs forward, verifies max angle error < 1e-3 rad vs fp64 reference\n\nFixes #8842\n\nSigned-off-by: Siddhant Rajhans <sidjha88@gmail.com>",
